From 6f1832c967502011877be6b076b624cddab3821d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Jun 2025 17:49:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 261/913] dts: stm32: use correct SPI for parent of EXTI 19 for
 stm32mp13

EXTI node for stm32mp13 in OP-TEE must use the RTC_WKUP_ALARM_S (SPI 128),
i.e. RTC wakeup timer and alarms (A and B) secure interrupt as source of
EXTI 19 = RTC wakeup timer and alarm (A and B) wakeup
(ORed non-secure: RTC_WKUP_ALARM_S, SPI 3
 and      secure: RTC_WKUP_ALARM_S, SPI 128).

Linux use the non secure interrupt but OP-TEE must use the secure
interruption so we have a difference in STM32MP13 Soc device tree
between secure and non secure world on this interrupt line.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git d549dd6331a371c4950ce6ce792babfc70afc194 dts: stm32: use correct SPI for parent of EXTI 19 for stm32mp13]
Fixes: 1b9cc51c2d54 ("dts: stm32: align EXTI nodes to upstream bindings on stm32mp131")
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iaa3bcefe8af91755af92b0a5e67290928a18ee9c
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/467035
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Antonio Maria BORNEO <antonio.borneo@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp131.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp131.dtsi b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp131.dtsi
index f1bd7c39c..8d5a1ff07 100644
--- a/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp131.dtsi
+++ b/core/arch/arm/dts/stm32mp131.dtsi
@@ -303,7 +303,7 @@
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 1   IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				<0>,
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 128 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
-				<&intc GIC_SPI 3   IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				<&intc GIC_SPI 129 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				<0>,						/* EXTI_20 */
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 32  IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 				<&intc GIC_SPI 34  IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
